his is a must see", "text": "The experience there is astonishing. You'll be able to see the hindu rites along the river. This is very emotional and you'll never forget it for sure.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2017-12-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "C3161CF033A084DCFA1B44EFB8F5D374", "name": "Florian N", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/611floriann", "username": "611floriann", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/11/87/48/2e/florian-n.jpg", "contribution_count": 3, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-02-03", "published_at_date": "2018-02-04"}, {"review_id": 557929121, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r557929121-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Not worth the money!", "text": "The temple itself must be beautiful, but paying 1000 NRs to walk around the patio and see monkeys (not even well looked after monkeys, there was a dead baby monkey!!) is a total rob. I'd understand maybe half of that to support the maintenance but paying that amount of money and then not even be allowed to see the temple (which looked incredible peering from the door) because we are not hindu is absolutely ridiculous! \nSpeaking with Hindu friends I've understood the religious never forbid entrance to temples to people of other religions so I find this ban real nonsense. I'd understand not entering with cameras, touching or certain behaviours but I recommend people not to enter the \"temple\" area and proceed directly to the crematory.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 1, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo",